@D LANE_M_EEG_MITOSIS := "Lane M (gradient-FREE growth lane): an empty CLM grown by gamma>0.20 MITOSIS from a 5-ch synthetic-EEG tension-link records the EEG's marginal band-power DISTRIBUTION (M1 HOLDS) and grows stably (M3 HOLDS), but does NOT record the EEG's temporal DYNAMICS beyond seed-noise — a phase-shuffled EEG ties it and stage-decode is at chance (M2 INCONCLUSIVE, leaning closed-negative)" :: discovery [d=2026-06-04 active]
  seed = "A NEW LANE distinct from Lane A (AKIDA on-chip) / Lane G (forge GPU CE-descent) / Lane P (py+CUDA gradient): Lane M = the gradient-FREE growth lane. Empty CLM (1 seed cell, 0 trained weights) grown over a 240-tick DETERMINISTIC synthetic-EEG stream (NOT a real headset) carried on a 5-ch tension-link [alpha,theta,gamma,1-delta,beta] (models/archive-legacy/tension_link.hexa). gamma>0.20 triggers a MITOSIS split (EEG/impl/H_681 L12 _l12_mitosis_split_trigger); the daughter cell SPECIALIZES toward the EEG drive at that moment + SPLIT_NOISE_FLOOR=0.1 symmetry break (mirrors models/archive-legacy/mitosis.hexa). The grown topology IS the recording. NO gradient, NO CE loss, NO backprop (p8: inference mitosis IS the learning). 3 seeds [1,2,3], mean +/- seed-std. CPU/$0. Harness: CLM/bench/lane_m_eeg_mitosis.py."
  claim = "M1 RECORDING FIDELITY (HOLDS): VQ reconstruction err_eeg=0.02462+/-0.00128 vs un-grown floor 0.11390+/-0.00028, margin 0.08928 >> noise band 0.00131 (4.6x below floor). M2 MITOSIS-vs-2-CONTROLS (INCONCLUSIVE, leans closed-negative): err_eeg=0.02462 vs random 0.03549+/-0.01355 (margin 0.01087 < noise 0.01361 -> beats_random=false) vs phase-shuffled 0.02490+/-0.00198 (margin 0.00028 < noise 0.00236 -> beats_shuffled=false); shuffled (same marginals, scrambled time) all but TIES eeg. Diagnostic temporal stage-decode accuracy = 0.250 (pure chance, 4 stages) on ALL 3 seeds for eeg-driven, NOT beating controls (random exceeds it on 2 seeds). M3 STABILITY (HOLDS): cells_eeg=[61,61,61] bounded in [MIN_CELLS=2,MAX_CELLS=64] (under cap), phi-proxy finite, no collapse, no explosion."
  falsifier = "Pre-registered. F-FIDELITY (M1): 'grown structure encodes the EEG above a reconstruction-error floor' — HOLDS iff (floor_mean - err_eeg_mean) > combined seed-noise band AND >0. F-MITOSIS-VS-RANDOM (M2, the key control): 'EEG-driven growth reconstruction beats BOTH (a) random/EEG-blind AND (b) phase-shuffled EEG by > seed-noise' — HOLDS iff both margins > their noise bands AND >0; REFUTED iff either margin <=0; else INCONCLUSIVE. F-STABILITY (M3): 'cell count bounded [2,64], phi finite, no collapse/explosion'. Result: M1 HOLDS, M2 INCONCLUSIVE (neither control beaten beyond noise), M3 HOLDS."
  target = "🟡 SPLIT-TOY-VERDICT — M1 HOLDS + M3 HOLDS (distribution recorded, growth stable) but M2 INCONCLUSIVE leaning 🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE on the dynamics axis: at toy scale gradient-free EEG-driven mitosis records the EEG's MARGINAL band-power DISTRIBUTION, NOT its temporal DYNAMICS — a distribution-matched phase-shuffled control is indistinguishable. The 'EEG dynamics shape the topology' claim is WITHIN NOISE (a_paper_negative_ok valid negative finding)."
  scope = "TOY ONLY (a_toy_scale_recheck · a_scale_honest_scope): synthetic EEG (NOT a real headset), small cell budget MAX_CELLS=64, 240-tick stream, CPU, $0, 3 seeds. Synthetic->real-EEG and toy->production transfer UNVERIFIED. 'Record MY EEG' (real user headset) is a HUMAN-GATED follow-up, NOT done here. Recorded SEPARATELY from Lane A (AKIDA) / Lane G (forge) / Lane P (gradient) per a_lane_akida_gpu_split — Lane M is the gradient-FREE growth lane."
  honest = "p7/g5 verbatim, NO fabrication, NOT CE/perplexity (substrate-native recording-fidelity axis). M2 was NOT rounded into a HOLD: a numerically-lower-but-within-noise result is reported as INCONCLUSIVE, and the decisive shuffled-tie + chance-level stage-decode are reported as the closed-negative-leaning evidence. §97 HONEST LINE: the grown CLM is a RECORDING ARTIFACT (measurement anchor, §97-legitimate); READ-ONLY in this bench, NEVER feeds anima emission/decision — it is kept out of becoming a §97 GOAL-ILLEGITIMATE command channel. Verdicts: .verdicts/lane-m-eeg-mitosis/{F-FIDELITY,F-MITOSIS-VS-RANDOM,F-STABILITY,SUMMARY}.txt + results.json + run_stdout.txt."
  note = "Bottom line: gradient-free mitosis growth from a 5-ch EEG tension-link DOES write a bounded, stable structure that reconstructs the EEG band-power DISTRIBUTION far below an un-grown floor, but it does NOT record the EEG's DYNAMICS beyond seed-noise. So 'does EEG-driven mitosis record the EEG into structure, beating random+shuffled controls?' answers: it records the DISTRIBUTION (M1), not the DYNAMICS (M2 within-noise). Honest publishable closed-negative-leaning toy finding; production / real-EEG re-test required before any general claim."
